---
title: Frontend Architecture for GEO & AEO
description: Research dashboard for investigating how frontend architecture affects generative search.
---

{% hero %}

## Research workspace

Investigating how frontend architecture influences the machine readability, content extractability, retrievability, answerability, and citation potential of web content in generative search and answer systems.

### Research objective

Develop technology-independent, evidence-based frontend architecture guidelines. Keep scientific findings, empirical observations, plausible recommendations, and unverified assumptions clearly distinguished.

{% /hero %}

{% research-cards %}

## Status at a glance

{% research-card title="Current phase" lead="Foundation and research design" %}
All six hypotheses and four experiments are **proposed**. No experiment results or research findings have been recorded.
{% /research-card %}

{% research-card title="Progress" lead="1 of 5 lifecycle stages initialized" %}
{% progress value=1 max=5 label="Research lifecycle progress" /%} Research framing is initialized. A targeted [HtmlRAG source appraisal](/en/03-notes/paper-notes/htmlrag/) is available; systematic evidence synthesis, experiment execution, project-result analysis, and guideline validation remain pending.
{% /research-card %}

{% research-card title="Next steps" lead="Before data collection" %}
1. Finalize and version the scoping-review search, screening, and extraction protocol before running searches.
2. Freeze experiment estimands, primary outcomes, annotation rules, analysis plans, and pilot-based sample-size rationale.
3. Pilot one experiment end to end; inspect parity, measurement reliability, and pipeline failures before scaling.
4. Select tools only after the measures and reproducibility requirements are specified.
{% /research-card %}

{% research-card title="Open research questions" lead="Methodological questions" %}
- Which crawler and retrieval pipelines can be measured reproducibly?
- How can content extraction quality be separated from answer-generation quality?
- Which confounding variables must be controlled across rendering variants?
- How can source citation behavior be evaluated independently of answer correctness?
{% /research-card %}

{% /research-cards %}

{% section %}

## Active research

The current focus is to establish a reproducible literature review and controlled studies of semantics, rendering, structured data, and content architecture. No experimental results are available yet.

{% /section %}

{% section %}

## Active hypotheses

The initial hypotheses are proposals, not established results.

{% toggletip id="status-legend" label="What do the statuses mean?" %}
{% terms %}
{% term name="Proposed" %}Formulated for testing; no appraised evidence is linked yet.{% /term %}
{% term name="Under Investigation" %}Literature appraisal or an experiment is in progress; no conclusion has been drawn.{% /term %}
{% term name="Supported" %}Linked, documented evidence is consistent with the hypothesis within its stated scope.{% /term %}
{% term name="Rejected" %}Linked, documented evidence contradicts the hypothesis within its stated scope.{% /term %}
{% term name="Inconclusive" %}Evidence is available but insufficient or mixed; it neither supports nor rejects the hypothesis.{% /term %}
{% /terms %}
{% /toggletip %}

