## Evidence overview

Evidence has not yet been evaluated. All initial hypotheses remain proposed; no A, B, or C evidence level has been justified. Levels are assigned as follows:

{% terms %}
{% term name="A — Strong evidence" %}Multiple high-quality independent studies or robust empirical evidence.{% /term %}
{% term name="B — Good evidence" %}Empirical evidence with some limitations.{% /term %}
{% term name="C — Limited or indirect evidence" %}Related research, limited experiments, or indirect findings.{% /term %}
{% term name="D — Hypothesis / unverified" %}Plausible assumptions or research questions without sufficient evidence.{% /term %}
{% /terms %}

{% /section %}

